---
// Bring-your-own-models proof: each agent on the plan or key you gave it.
---

<div
  class="tg-card tg"
  role="img"
  aria-label="Illustrative Telegram exchange: you ask klanker what it runs on. It replies that it uses a Claude plan login that belongs to it alone, and that no API key is configured as a fallback. Other agents can run on Codex, OpenRouter or a local model."
>
  <div class="tg-head" aria-hidden="true">
    <span class="back">‹</span>
    <span class="who"><b>klanker</b><span>bot</span></span>
    <span class="tg-ava a4">k</span>
  </div>
  <div class="tg-body" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="msg out tail">
      <p>what are you running on?</p>
      <span class="meta">14:05 <span class="ticks">✓✓</span></span>
    </div>
    <div class="msg in tail" style="max-width:92%">
      <span class="name">klanker</span>
      <p class="card-title">🔌 My model</p>
      <div class="rows">
        <span class="row"><span class="st ok">✓</span><span>Model: <b>Claude</b>, on a plan login</span></span>
        <span class="row"><span class="st ok">✓</span><span>That login is mine alone</span></span>
        <span class="row"><span class="st ok">✓</span><span>API key fallback: <b>none set</b></span></span>
      </div>
      <p>Other agents can be on Codex, OpenRouter or a local model.</p>
      <span class="meta">14:05</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
